<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter III of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1239–<a href="/years/1285">1285</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Peter the Great of Aragon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter III was king of Aragon from 1276. Married to Constance, heiress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Sicilian Vespers</a> of 1282, beginning the long Aragonese rule of the island. He also took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albarracin">Albarracín</a> in 1284 and repelled a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against Aragon in 1285, the year he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Peter III of Aragon" width="250" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Villani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_III_rey_de_Arag%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
